WEBVTT

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.530
Took you long enough...

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.150
I guess you finally noticed me.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.210
Your terror, yes... I can see it!

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.050
That's right... struggle! Struggle!

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.740
The color of your pathetic 
clinging to life...

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.890
Show it to me...

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:36.840
That dirty, ugly color!

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:14.110
<b>May 2nd, 2001 - Alaska
Onboard an UN Army An-225 Mriya</b>

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.270
Look at that! The Yukon River!

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:20.680
What trials will the goddess 
of Alaska bestow on us?

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.530
Ensign Bridges?

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.910
Have some salmon eggs and 
take a nap or something.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.990
That's right. We can probably 
catch all kinds of king salmon.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:30.530
And get piles of salmon eggs... Or not!

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.950
Listen, we're here representing America.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.520
Let's do our country proud.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.050
Or you could just call it a demotion.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.860
Don't be such a grouch.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.480
Yukon Base has TSFs from all over the world.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.680
It's like a dream come true, right?

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.530
Yuuya Bridges!

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.800
I'm never flying with you again.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.310
You asshole!

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.280
I wouldn't fly with you anyway!

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.750
What's going on?

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.540
We're already on an approach course!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:08.910
Yukon control, come in!

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.330
Damn it!

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.590
Why? Why can't I shake them off?

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.980
Argo 3, return to base now.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.930
Permission for mock combat 
has not been given.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:30.880
Repeat.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.580
Permission for mock combat 
has not been given.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.480
Shut up!

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.950
They're serious!

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.320
If I stop here they'll seriously kill me!

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.800
Two TSFs have left the training zone and
are approaching you from the rear.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.940
What's is going on?

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.300
Damn it! What the hell are they doing here?

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.070
Exit your approach and stand 
by at a higher altitude.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.070
Hey, get out of here!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:53.150
This sound... one, no, two TSFs?

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.380
Hey!

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.180
You think you're such 
hot stuff? Not for long!

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.480
Take...

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.940
Don't climb!

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:16.980
Head straight for the runway!

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.550
...this!

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.550
No way...

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.300
This must be what "happiness" feels like.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.540
You saved us.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.440
I guess you really do belong at Yukon Base.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.520
They're making those things?

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:06.280
Damn it... damn it!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.430
So I can kill you now?

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:11.510
How wonderful...

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.400
Where are they?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.120
Where'd they go?

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.210
No!

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.840
<b>Verdant Yukon</b>

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.710
Hey, you okay?

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:38.810
Hang in there!

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:48.630
I'll get you yet, damn it!

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.910
Idar-1 to command post.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.960
We've confirmed the survival 
of the crashed pilot.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:53.830
Roger.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.290
Return to base.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.010
Idar-1, roger.

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.280
I'm scared...

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.470
I'm scared, Cryska.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.590
She crashed.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.470
She might be hurt.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:05.710
Don't worry.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:06.940
She's safe.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.590
I've already confirmed it.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.750
Are we going to crash too?

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.720
Is our TSF going to crash like hers did?

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.630
Don't worry. He won't.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.150
Neither will you and I.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.420
Really?

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.900
Really.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:27.040
I'll always protect you, Inia.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.610
Always.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:29.970
Okay?

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.450
Yeah...

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:38.330
Wow!

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:43.800
The Jian-10 from the Chinese United Front, 
and the European Union's Tornado!

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:47.070
They were taking promotional 
photos of the TSFs today.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:53.850
I guess they really are bringing pilots 
and TSFs from all over the world.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.090
That's right.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.970
We're gonna kill all those BETA assholes.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.960
The Next-Generation TSF 
Technology Development Plan.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.490
AKA Project Prominence.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.740
The UN has offered Yukon Base as a 
place for militaries all over the world

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:13.320
who've lost their own nations 
to develop their TSF technology.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:17.370
It's most important goal is to bring test 
pilots and prototypes together from every nation,

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:23.920
so that shared information and technology 
can accelerate TSF development.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.060
Are TSFs that new to you?

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:29.660
What obscure backwater are you from?

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:35.180
I suppose you could describe Groom 
Lake, Nevada as a backwater.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:38.080
So I was right, huh.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.030
You've never heard of Area 51?

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:43.470
It's America's biggest research base.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.640
You mean America's biggest theme park, right?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.540
If you've got a mech pilot's wing mark, 
does that mean you're an Eishi?

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.430
Yeah.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.850
Show some gratitude.

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:56.820
If it wasn't for him you would've gone BOOM!

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.950
You did that?

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:03.080
No. You dodged us.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.420
T-That's right.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.110
You hicks should respect your betters.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:14.180
More importantly, what's the 
pilot of that Terminator like?

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.740
D-Don't ask me...

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:23.280
My... Everything's so big in this country.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:28.120
I guess I'll have to call 
somebody to come pick me up.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:29.720
Are you lost?

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.700
It's not this way, it's that way.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.280
Oh.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.050
I guess you caught me in 
an embarrassing moment.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:40.980
The command post...

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:42.840
You just got here, I know.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.870
Your color told me so.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.430
<b>UN Pacific Theatre Force 3 - Yukon Army Base General Command</b>

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.800
She's Japanese?

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:20.680
First I'll introduce the new team members.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.530
Ensign Yuuya Bridges.

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:25.710
From the American military's 
tactical studies squad.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.100
An elite Eishi.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:31.000
And Ensign Stella Bremer, from Sweden.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.210
Ensign Valerio Giacosa from Italy.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:37.450
Ensign Tarisa Manandal from Nepal.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:43.100
And this is Lt. Yui Takamura, 
from the Imperial Japanese army.

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:48.520
Lastly, I am Ibrahim Dogulu from Turkey.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.270
My rank is Lieutenant.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:53.020
I am the captain of the Argos Flight.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:58.530
Our squad will be working on the XFJ project.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.690
The XFJ project is...

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:09.590
The XFJ project is we at Boening's attempt 
to improve the Japanese military's type-94...

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.910
Oh, excuse me.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:18.740
This is Frank Heinemann, a technical 
advisor with Boening Corporation.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:20.300
Welcome, everyone.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:26.760
And the goal of today's exercises is for you 
XFJ project members to get to know each other.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.010
Lieutenant.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:30.060
Will we be infiltrating Lilfort?

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:31.120
No.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:32.560
Something better.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.540
Case 47.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:40.800
The combat area will be 
considered 170 kilometers south

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:43.250
of a BETA controlled zone 
filled with laser class,

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:43.700
A Turkish captain...

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:46.560
and so altitude restrictions 
will be in effect.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:46.850
Italy.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:49.530
The win condition is to shoot 
down the other team's leader.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:49.960
Sweden.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:52.960
In addition, both teams will start 
with a destroyed command post.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.530
Vanguards will go with AH3 equipment.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.920
Interceptors with AH6.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:57.920
Nepal.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.900
Your tactical database will be restricted to information on your teammate's units.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:59.850
And...

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:07.470
All from countries who've lost 
their territory to the BETA, huh?

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:11.890
Joint US-Japanese project? Hah!

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:15.770
That covers the details.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.720
I'll announce the teams.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:19.680
Element A.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.160
Ensign Giacosa.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.150
Ensign Manandal.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.350
Element B.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:26.680
Ensign Bremer.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:27.980
Ensign Bridges.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:31.790
Ensign Bridges will take the 
captain's TSF in my place.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.520
Wait!

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.660
What is it, Ensign Manandal?

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:38.060
Excuse me.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.100
Why is he in the leader unit?

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:44.600
Ensign Bridges is the main 
pilot of the XFJ plan.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.360
You're kidding me.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.310
Again?

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:55.220
Everyone be in your TSFs and 
ready to launch by 1325.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.330
That is all.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.670
Dismissed.

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:05.070
Jeez.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.760
How come he gets to be in the captain's TSF?

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.570
I feel bad for you, Stella.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.790
You have to watch over the new kid.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.120
Really?

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.710
I think he's good looking, if nothing else.

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.320
Are you serious?

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:20.090
So that's your type, Stella?

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:26.640
Well, I can knock that 
hick out in 30 seconds.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:29.520
You shouldn't let your guard down.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.140
He was the test pilot for the Raptor.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:37.110
It doesn't matter.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:40.360
I'll have him go through 
the Argos Flight's baptism.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.860
I'll look forward to it.

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:49.870
So what brings an elite US pilot out here?

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:52.690
A lot of things.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:54.750
A lot of things, huh?

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.650
A girl?

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:58.630
I refuse to accept it!

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:01.210
I don't care if it's an order.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:05.830
I refuse to accept that you're 
piloting the captain's unit.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:07.630
Hey, calm down.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:08.640
Shut up, VG.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:11.710
For starters, you...

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:13.140
You pilot the captain's unit then.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.400
I'm not taking your orders.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.140
You think you're giving me 
a handicap or something?

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:22.070
Don't insult me!

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.770
I've never piloted an Active before.

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:29.520
We'll both be able to perform 
better in the TSFs we're used to.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:30.350
Right?

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.750
Fine.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.570
If you insist, I'll switch places with you.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:36.510
Okay.

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:43.200
Is there still something else?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.810
Say thank you!

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:49.150
I swapped with you because you insisted!

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:50.880
Right, right.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:55.980
Don't come whining to me later!

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.340
Hey, Yuuya!

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.350
Don't change your position 
without asking the captain.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:04.920
Think about the mechanics...

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.960
Status parameter adjustment 
error is within 1%.

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.700
Good work, Vincent.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.200
Oh. Well, thanks.

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:15.450
I'm the only one who could do 
this much tuning this fast.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.650
Bye.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:18.210
Okay, go kick some butt!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:10.410
We will now begin versus-human 
tactical training.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:11.850
Begin operation.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.590
Command post to all Argos units.

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.600
Please begin the operation.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.030
Argos 4, found them yet?

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:24.220
Not yet.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.550
There's a lot of noisemakers.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.530
The filtering can't keep up.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:29.920
So we have to rely on optics, huh?

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:32.310
Keep trying to locate the enemy.

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:33.750
Argos 4. Roger.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.440
Ensign Bremer.

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:37.500
A word.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:38.370
What is it?

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:41.090
I've no intention of losing.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.140
I'm an Eishi, too.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:46.300
Of course, I'm going to win this.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.270
Yeah.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:54.420
Let's see what you Alaskan 
hicks can do, Argos Flight.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.240
Let's get started, Top Gun?

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.810
Who are you calling Top Gun?

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:04.530
What's wrong?

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:08.020
Wasn't the American military supposed to have 
the best ranged weapon technology in the world?

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:09.820
Come out and I'll show you.

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:12.820
He's moving so well in a confined space.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:16.270
You can turn up the heat a little.

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:18.640
I'm surprised you were the vanguard.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.330
I thought it'd be Chobi.

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:28.960
Pay attention when you're 
on the battlefield, hick!

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:32.170
VG, he's my target!

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:32.840
Drop back!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.280
I guess you're an elite at running.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.460
An Active's got the 
advantage in acceleration.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.840
Let's corner him, VG!

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:42.600
Roger!

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:47.950
Oh my, I missed?

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.160
That was a close call.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:51.780
She's got good timing.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.570
Now it's our turn.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.140
You're in the way, VG!

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:03.210
You cover Stella!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.620
I'll handle him.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.360
Right, right.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.700
Whatever you want.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:12.080
Not bad, hick!

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:12.500
Next!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.010
Roger.

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:15.300
Tarisa!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.550
Argos 2, 300 36mm rounds remaining.

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:23.060
Why won't they hit?

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.290
Argos 3 and 4 moving to area D.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.820
Argos 1, error in right main arm.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.800
Ensign Yuuya Bridges.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.970
I guess he's as good as his 
record suggests, but...

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:35.320
He's at the disadvantage against an Active.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.950
This is more my taste than some guy.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:41.740
It's gonna cost you.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.740
Don't worry. It always does.

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:45.650
Come on, Chobi.

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:47.000
You got that one on one fight you wanted.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.000
I'll finish it at close range.

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:54.210
I'm at a disadvantage when climbing.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.560
Hey, stop running!

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.550
It won't hit me!

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:10.730
You'll pay for that, you hick bastard!

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:13.900
Give it up already!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:17.070
Just let me beat you!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.610
Don't be in such a rush, Chobi.

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:27.280
Impressive, Ensign Bridges.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:30.040
Not a situation I'd like to find myself in.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:34.540
Ensign Manandal especially is 
an expert at close-range combat.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.760
This wasn't my plan, but 
I'll go along with it!

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:41.760
Sounds good.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.690
Don't think I'll let you get behind me!

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:58.940
I've seen it!

00:18:59.180 --> 00:18:59.950
What?

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:08.290
Girls don't like guys who are too persistent.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:10.740
I've been like this since I was born.

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:11.820
I can't help it.

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.210
You're inviting me in again?

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.380
It's hard being a popular guy.

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:19.920
Did you give up?

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.480
Sorry, Tarisa.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.470
Ain't it great?

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:32.020
Now you'll be able to go 
back to Nevada, Mr. Elite.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.190
I'm never flying with you again!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:45.270
I'll give you credit for knocking me over.

00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:49.490
Fire.

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.880
So she just made it.

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:05.430
Argos 2. Damage to head and chest cockpit.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.680
The damage has destroyed your TSF.

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:08.680
Ho-

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.070
Mission complete.

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:12.390
Everyone, return to the start point.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.400
How?

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:21.120
Thanks for bringing her somewhere 
that's easy to target.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.670
So you trusted Stella despite 
never teaming with her before?

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.240
Brave man.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.660
We had shared interests, that's all.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:31.560
Well, no matter how good you 
are, you can't win alone.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:32.740
Right, Tarisa?

00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:34.990
You need to keep up, VG!

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:36.920
You call that teamwork?

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.300
You think a Strike can 
keep up with an Active?

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:43.840
And you're the one who 
told me to follow Stella.

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:49.080
Don't get cocky!

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.710
I was winning when it was just us!

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:53.970
I told you it's a team battle.

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:56.040
We're just better.

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:56.930
Right?

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:57.960
Yeah.

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:02.890
I guess we learned a lesson from the Top Gun.

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:05.770
Stop calling me Top Gun, Macaroni.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.700
Are you calling me Macaroni?

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:11.130
Call me VG.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.490
Valerio Giacosa, VG are my initials.

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:15.150
Got it, Macaroni.

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:16.300
Hey there.

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:19.380
Top Gun and Macaroni, huh?

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.730
I like it.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.590
Don't laugh, Chobi.

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:24.970
That's right, Chobi.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:26.540
You're cute, Chobi.

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:29.340
Who are you calling Chobi?

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:30.960
You.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:34.600
What? Yuuya's handing out nicknames already?

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:35.660
Nicknames?

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.200
It's a talent of his.

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.110
Hey, what's my nickname?

00:21:43.090 --> 00:21:45.360
It's probably giant tits or somet-

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:51.120
Venus, maybe?

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:54.440
I'm honored.

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:00.480
Okay then, once more.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:03.290
Welcome to Argos Flight...

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:04.620
Top Gun.

00:22:06.610 --> 00:22:08.470
Thanks.

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:13.720
I saw that last battle of yours.

00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:24.320
Did you enjoy seeing the latest in 
American combat manuverability, Lt.?

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:27.370
I suppose the Empire's TSFs...

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:28.950
I'm disappointed, Ensign Bridges.

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:34.280
To think I have to entrust the future 
of the Empire to someone like you...

00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:39.370
What did you say?

00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.590
You Japanese doll!

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:07.490
I'll make this easy to understand.

00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:09.300
You're inexperienced.

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:11.830
Just who are they anyway?

00:24:12.100 --> 00:24:14.820
Inia and Cryska, was it?

00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:18.250
They really looked cold, didn't they?

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:24.310
<b>A Flock of Hazy Moons</b>

00:24:19.190 --> 00:24:23.560
Next time on Total Eclipse: 
A Flock of Hazy Moons
